    "id": "rk_370c056edd24ee93f8d6",
    "text": "Important limit: do not flatten these women into \"sexual sinners.\" In Genesis 38, the text vindicates Tamar over Judah. Ruth is presented positively. Bathsheba's degree of agency in 2 Samuel 11 is debated and the power imbalance with David is substantial. Matthew's wording \"wife of Uriah\" places David's compromised history in the genealogy rather than erasing it.",
