    "id": "rk_5fff4b06d7d8cb619f8e",
    "text": "Matthew 1:18–19 says Mary is betrothed to Joseph, calls Joseph her husband, and says he considers divorcing/dismissing her. This fits a two-stage marital process in which betrothal was already legally binding even before the couple began living together. The point is visible from Matthew itself: a mere modern engagement would not require divorce terminology.",
