    "id": "rk_61440093ff8086c52bd7",
    "text": "Deuteronomy 34 — Moses's death. The chapter records his burial in an unknown location with the notation \"no one knows his burial place to this day.\" The phrase \"to this day\" supplies evidence of a later perspective looking backward and is incompatible with Moses narrating the chapter in its present form. Traditional harmonizations assign the chapter to Joshua or another later hand.  Calling that move “special pleading” is an evaluation of the harmonization, not a historical finding; the historical observation is only that the chapter contains post-Mosaic narration.",
    "raw_text": "**Deuteronomy 34 — Moses's death.** The chapter records his burial in an unknown location with the notation \"no one knows his burial place to this day.\" The phrase \"to this day\" supplies evidence of a later perspective looking backward and is incompatible with Moses narrating the chapter in its present form. Traditional harmonizations assign the chapter to Joshua or another later hand. ⟨INFERENCE⟩ Calling that move “special pleading” is an evaluation of the harmonization, not a historical finding; the historical observation is only that the chapter contains post-Mosaic narration.",
