    "id": "rk_5453711af5f33dd6cc1f",
    "text": "Camp split on how to read Paul's move: the critical/New Perspective reading (Sanders, Dunn, Wright — N.T. Wright, already on file at §9.5/Field Guide §19.8) treats it as genuine reconfiguration — covenant membership redefined around faith rather than law. The conservative-evangelical continuity reading treats Pauline universalism as fulfillment rather than innovation; Kaiser's position above is naturally read this way — if OT mission already carried centrifugal impulses, Paul's move is a continuation, not a break.",
